---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Terms of use for the Slumbio iPhone app. Apple's standard EULA governs
// the download; this covers the subscription and the obvious disclaimers.
const updated = 'September 2026';
---

<Base title="Terms · Slumbio" description="Terms of use for the Slumbio app." noindex puck={false}>
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">Slumbio · updated {updated}</p>
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="lede">Short, because there is not much to say.</p>
  </header>

  <section class="body">
    <h2>The app</h2>
    <p>
      Slumbio is provided by Brett Boggs. Your download is governed by Apple's
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/">standard licensed application end user license agreement</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Not medical advice</h2>
    <p>
      Slumbio plays sound, guides breathing and shares general notes on sleep.
      None of it is medical advice, diagnosis or treatment. If sleep has been a
      problem for weeks, or you have a heart or breathing condition, talk to a
      doctor before using breathing exercises. Do not use the app while
      driving or doing anything that needs your attention.
    </p>

    <h2>Slumbio Plus</h2>
    <p>
      Plus is available as a yearly subscription, a monthly subscription, or a
      one-time lifetime purchase, all through Apple's in-app purchase system
      at the prices shown in the app. Subscriptions renew automatically unless
      cancelled at least 24 hours before the end of the current period, and
      your Apple Account is charged for renewal within 24 hours before the
      period ends. The yearly plan may include a free introductory week; if
      you do not cancel before it ends, the subscription begins and you are
      charged. Manage or cancel any time in Settings › Apple Account ›
      Subscriptions on your phone. Refunds are handled by Apple under Apple's
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Alarms</h2>
    <p>
      The sunrise alarm depends on the app running and playing sound. iOS can
      stop a background app at any time. A backup notification is scheduled,
      but do not rely on Slumbio as your only alarm for anything that
      matters.
    </p>

    <h2>Warranty and liability</h2>
    <p>
      The app is provided as is, without warranties of any kind. To the extent
      the law allows, Brett Boggs is not liable for any loss arising from your
      use of the app.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>These terms may change. The date at the top is the current version.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="mailto:brettmboggs@gmail.com">brettmboggs@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <a class="back-link" href="/slumbio/">&larr; Slumbio</a>
</Base>

<style>
  .body {
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 3rem;
  }
  .body h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
  }
  .body p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
</style>
